## Diagnosis (deliverable 1): the provenance session token hashed into every index leaf

**Exact locus.** The divergent manifest field is all four `:indexes` root addresses (`:eavt`/`:aevt`/`:avet`/`:vaet`); `:count` and `:branching-factor` (512) agree. One datom per transaction differs: `[meta-e :yin.repl/session <shell-token> t m]` minted in [packet->tx-data](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:116). The token is `(str (random-uuid))` per shell in [create-state](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:926), passed as `:session-token` in [make-session](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:790). Each test session (`session` in [stream_eval_test.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/clojure/stream_eval_test.cljc:31)) therefore indexes the same 15 programs with a different token string.

**Propagation chain.** Token datom → memory-log transaction record → [snapshot-datoms](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc:464) → all four B-trees (every datom is in every index) → leaf blobs `{:keys [...]}` containing the token UTF-8 → leaf/branch/root segment addresses → manifest `{:indexes {...} :count n :branching-factor 512}` in [publish-index!](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc:619) (and the incremental [publish!](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc:1172)) → `(jing/segment-key manifest)` at [yin/repl/index.cljc:410](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:410) (blake3 over canonical CBOR). Fifteen distinct token datoms (one per round, same string) poison every leaf, so all four roots and the manifest address differ, fresh every run — matching the relay's "different hash set per run."

**Ruled out.** CBOR sorts map keys/set elements by canonical bytes ([cbor.cljc:794](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc:794)); bulk build sorts before shaping ([from-sequential](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/data/btree.cljc:2059)); frontend temporaries are positional `dsg__` names ("lowering is deterministic," [yang/clojure.cljc:167](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:167)); row ids are content keys ([vm.cljc:1155](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:1155)). Stream identities and the expander token ([repl.cljc:738](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:738)) appear only in cursors and the dropped macro log packet, never in tree rows; the test's `strip` already normalizes the cursor UUID. The token is intentional provenance ("Record its stable shell token as a fact," [yin.repl.dao.space-index.md:45](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.repl.dao.space-index.md:45)), and the equivalence test holds the token fixed (`"equivalence"`, [index_test.cljc:319](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/repl/index_test.cljc:319)) — equivalence was only ever proven per-token. Regression window: `:index-publication` (with `:manifest-address`) entered `repl-state` in `3c301b65`; before that, summaries carried no address and parity held.

