## Proposed minimal fix (deliverable 3): stop publishing the provenance-bearing address in the serializable summary

In [repl.cljc:2209](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:2209), drop `:manifest-address` from `:index-publication` (keep `:cursor :transactions`); update the pinning assertion at [index_test.cljc:288](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/repl/index_test.cljc:288) to match. Rationale: the manifest address correctly hashes provenance-bearing content — changing indexed datoms would break provenance queries, recovery ("Restored facts keep their original session tokens"), and HEAD/DHT semantics, which all read the indexer directly, not `repl-state`. The token-independence contract already exists for reporting ([status](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:536): "never on … the shell's token"); the summary should honor it, exactly as the test already treats seals and medium identities as differing by design. Publication coverage is still cross-checked via cursor position plus transaction count.Completed-GMT: 2026-11-07 07:44:02 GMT
